<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Yule</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>look wheel
write
mail paper jolnir
touch pole
</pre>
<p>In December, the Yule Wheel, the year's wheel, stands in Udgaard's square. From 
December 1 to 24 one spoke turns each day: a small task somewhere in the world, 
for players of every level. look wheel shows the spokes still open and what to 
type for each. A spoke waits seven days after its day, so you can catch up on a 
week you missed.
</p><p>With 16 spokes you may wish for a gift from Jolnir, Odin as the Yule one. At a 
post office, type write, write your wish and end with @, then mail it to him 
(mail paper jolnir). He reads every letter you send, and grants one gift.
</p><p>From December 24 to 31, touch the pole in Udgaard's square, and Jolnir sees you 
in his hall. Kneel before him, and he gives you his gift, made for you. The more 
spokes you turned, the better it is: with all 24, it is the best your level 
allows, an artifact from level 100; with 16 to 23, one step less. look wheel 
tells you what yours would be.
</p><p>On Christmas Eve and Christmas Day, the sleigh elf in Udgaard's square takes you 
up in Santa's sleigh for a ride over the world (list, then hire sky).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
